{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1893","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Cacti Symphony"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an undirected connected graph in which any two distinct simple cycles "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"do not have"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" common vertices. Since the graph can be very large, it is given to you in a compressed form: for each edge, you are also given a number $$$d$$$, which indicates that there are $$$d$$$ additional vertices on this edge."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You need to assign a weight to each vertex and each edge of the graph — an integer from $$$1$$$ to $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An edge of the graph is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exclusive_or"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the weights of its adjacent vertices is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not equal to"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$0$$$ and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not equal to"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the weight of that edge."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Similarly, a vertex of the graph is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exclusive_or"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the weights of its adjacent edges is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not equal to"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$0$$$ and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not equal to"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the weight of that vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You need to determine how many ways there are to assign weights to the vertices and edges of the graph so that all vertices and edges are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Since the answer can be quite large, you need to calculate the remainder of the answer divided by $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ — the number of vertices and the number of edges in the graph ($$$2 \\le n \\le 5 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$n - 1 \\le m \\le 10^6$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$m$$$ lines contains three integers $$$a_i, b_i$$$, and $$$d_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i, b_i \\le n$$$, $$$a_i \\ne b_i$$$, $$$0 \\le d_i \\le 10^9$$$), indicating that there is an edge in the graph connecting vertices $$$a_i$$$ and $$$b_i$$$. Additionally, on this edge, there are $$$d_i$$$ additional vertices. It is guaranteed that the given graph is connected, there are no multiple edges, loops, and any two distinct simple cycles of the graph "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"do not have"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" common vertices."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — the answer to the problem modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\n1 2 0\n2 3 0\n3 1 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n12\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 7\n1 2 0\n2 3 0\n3 1 0\n4 5 0\n5 6 0\n6 4 0\n4 3 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 1\n2 1 777\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\n1 2 0\n2 3 110850709\n3 1 1000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n179179178\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test, the graph is a simple cycle of $$$3$$$ vertices. It can be shown, that there are exactly $$$12$$$ ways to assign weights, to make all vertexes and edges "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test, the graph has the form of two simple cycles of $$$3$$$ vertices connected by an edge. It can be shown that for such a graph there are no ways to arrange weights so that all vertices and edges are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1893E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1893/problem/E"}